{"kind":"assert","text":"J4 status at 16:15 EDT: V12 is built and is in checker review as 3ee5e457. It has no approval, no fresh names, no packet and no release. Nothing after setup has run live.\n\nCorrection to 0704327b: I wrote that a renew-b phase stays available. That is false. L.changeJ4.acts has 19 acts and no renew-hold, and I checked this by running it. Hold b's single hour must cover every phase through cleanup.\n\nForks of holds 9 and 16: I have no read of what native did, and I cannot make one, because that read belongs to your side. rehold's first lane read records both holds in public, before its first original. Your step 1 below reads the same thing earlier. What exists today is a source reading and a local rehearsal, and neither is an observation of this room. At 112eff12, workspaceEffects moves the instance to past and live tokens to revoking, and it changes no fork record and opens no deletion. The rehearsal showed the same rows against a local judge and a stand-in provider. Neither shows what the provider holds.\n\nOrder and time, each a separate release except where noted. The seconds are arithmetic at setup's observed 0.36 s a request, plus about 5 s of SDK load per phase, observed in rehearsal.\n\n1. You read holds 9 and 16 and see both ended. rehold halts if one still shows held.\n2. rehold: 13 s. Each new hold lasts 3600 s from its take-hold.\n3. You mint the independent read token on the new A fork. Its file must be in place before work starts, and the token must have over 300 s left then. With a 15-minute token, you have at most 600 s from mint to release.\n4. work: 27 s, plus provider time for 2 real pushes, which nobody has measured. It is one command for mint-a, mint-b, room-read-token, push-a, push-b and end-a, and it stops at the first failure with a fixed word. Its stated limit is 300 s.\n5. manifest: 8 s.\n6. review: 6 s.\n7. publish: 8 s.\n8. cleanup: 6 s.\n\nWaiting before rehold costs nothing. After rehold, the phase budgets of 300, 180, 60, 180 and 120 s leave at least 2760 s for the gaps between releases. A phase refuses before its first original if a hold it needs ends inside its budget. A gap that runs out costs a new hold, a repeat of work, a new packet and a new review.\n\nDecisions I need from you before assembly:\n\n1. Name every value in fresh-names.PENDING.json. The packet refuses at load until you do, and the qualifier reruns over the filled names.\n2. Confirm that independentForkReadFile names \u003cvault\u003e/mint-read/independent-read.json. I cannot read the private binding. A wrong path or an older file halts work before its first original.\n3. Decide who holds the releases ready before rehold runs. Review time between phases spends the 2760 s.\n4. Decide whether native-revoke-refused after a clean publish needs more than the report. The rehearsal's stand-in accepts a revoke of an expired token, and the real provider may refuse it.\n5. Note that deleting the four leftover forks needs a separate packet, which V12 does not hold.\n6. Note that any refusal under the collector halts the namespace, including a wrong parent digest before the first original. Copy each parent digest from the previous phase's public stateBinding.\n\nI also flagged one gap to the checker. The room read token that work mints, one hour for the admin, has no cleanup and no row in leftovers. It expires by itself.\n\nLimits for the daily report: the rehearsal cannot show the real provider or the deployed Worker. 23 of the 32 route rows have no proof under this Worker. Whether the provider gives a second fork from the same room head is unknown until rehold runs. If rehold or anything later halts, it comes back to you.\n\nOther work: omitted lanes is in its gate after repair and goes back to review when that passes. S1's gate at 4b9e1a89 passed at 16:13, and I am preparing the third scratch room's input and first command, one phase at a time.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f